#N canvas 40 40 780 520 12;
#X obj 30 90 c_clock 4 4;
#X obj 30 130 t b;
#X obj 30 170 f;
#X obj 90 170 + 1;
#X obj 30 220 mod 2;
#X obj 30 260 select 0 1;
#X msg 30 310 48;
#X msg 150 310 49;
#X obj 30 360 makenote 127 100;
#X obj 30 410 noteout 33;
#X text 30 20 404 BEAT DRIVER -- alternates bank A pad 1 and pad 2 on Cut It's OWN beat \, so the 404 is triggered by the instrument rather than by a free-running metro that would drift against it. A THROWAWAY TEST RIG \, not m_404: it makes no decisions \, publishes nothing \, and must not become the real mapping layer., f 92;
#X text 260 130 c_clock 4 4 IS AN INSTANCE \, NOT THE GLOBAL CLOCK -- ratio 4 to master \, so SIXTEENTH notes \, four to a bar. Outlet 1 is the beat bang -- outlet 0 is a signal phase and outlets 2-3 are beat number and bar. Using c_clock rather than a [del] off r clock is the point: the rate follows tempo for free and stays audio-domain \, which a message-clock delay would not., f 46;
#X text 260 240 mod 2 alternates: beat 0 and 2 -> A1 \, beat 1 and 3 -> A2. select 0 1 emits a BANG on each match \, so neither branch rides a reject outlet carrying data -- the trap this repo has hit four times., f 46;
#X text 260 380 CHANNEL 33 IS BANK A. The 404 is Pd device 3 on the Organelle \, so its block is 33-48 and each BANK gets its own channel: A=33 \, B=34 ... J=42. Note 48 is pad 1 \, note 49 is pad 2 -- the range is 36-51 \, NOT 47+n. Items 190-195., f 46;
#X text 30 450 ⚠️ ⚠️ RATIO x BPM MUST STAY UNDER 860 -- at ratio 4 that caps the tempo at 215 BPM. Above it threshold~ silently loses pulses and the beat SLOWS rather than erroring. At 120 BPM this fires 8 times a second \, alternating \, with a 100 ms note. That is deliberate: it is the heaviest MIDI the rig can be made to produce \, which is what makes it a power test rather than a demo., f 92;
